# Java and Spring

Follow `docs/engineering/development-standards.md` and
`docs/engineering/testing-quality-gates.md`.

- Keep package-by-feature and controller/application/domain/infrastructure
  boundaries from `LLD.md`.
- Controllers never access repositories directly, and persistence entities
  never become API responses.
- Use constructor injection, explicit imports, standard Java naming, UTF-8/LF,
  immutable dependencies, and the project formatter.
- Keep transactions in application services. Make queue publication and
  critical audit writes transactionally consistent.
- Enforce permission, organization, and object-level authorization at the
  application boundary and resource policy.
- Use safe repository APIs, parameterized queries, validated paths, bounded
  executors/queues/retries, and try-with-resources.
- Use structured, correlation-aware, redacted logging. Do not log and rethrow
  the same failure at every layer.
- Update OpenAPI and contract tests with API changes. Do not hand-edit
  generated clients.
- Use JUnit 5, modern Mockito, and JaCoCo. Test behavior, authorization,
  boundaries, failures, retries, and idempotency.
